\centering
\caption{Eight controversies: final placement (1 = best) under the observed rule and
under counterfactual combination rules R (rank), P (percentage), Z (z-scored), from
\texttt{controversy\_table.csv}.}
\label{tab:controversies}
\begin{tabular}{lccccc}
\toprule
Celebrity (season) & Observed & R & P & Z & Verdict \\
\midrule
Jerry Rice (S2)         & 2 & 2 & 2 & 2 & identical under both rules --- no method-attributable effect \\
Billy Ray Cyrus (S4)    & 5 & 5 & 5 & 7 & R and P agree with observed; Z would cut 2 weeks earlier \\
Bristol Palin (S11)     & 3 & 4 & 2 & 5 & under P she is runner-up (replayed P winner: Kyle Massey); R cuts her one week earlier \\
Bobby Bones (S27)       & 1 & 5 & 3 & 5 & neither rule reproduces the win; P gets closest (3rd) \\
Mya (S9)                & 2 & 2 & 1 & 1 & P/Z would have made Mya champion \\
Sabrina Bryan (S5)      & 7 & 7 & 7 & 7 & early S5 elimination predicted identically under every rule \\
Sabrina Bryan (S15)     & 8 & 3 & 8 & 2 & rank-style rules keep her to the finale (R 3rd / Z 2nd); the percentage-era exit is reproduced exactly under P \\
